    "mapping_notes": [
      "Complete publisher-edition poem (PTS/BJTS), not a line-complete translation of every VRI stanza. Whole-poem correspondence does not imply segment, line or word equivalence. Preserve independent VRI wording, variant notes and edition differences; do not invent missing words or transfer another poem’s refrain.",
      "Publisher main PTS heading391, BJTS brace/file394 and canonical tha-ap396 are separate literal identities. The Indus hermitage, Sumedha honey/mat offering, honey-rain rebirth narrative and named colophons establish this pair; no general number offset is approved.",
      "Retain local15–16/global3720 as one four-line source paragraph. Note21 distinguishes PTS two six-syllable-foot verses from BJTS one twelve-syllable-foot verse; local21 final numbering and20 printed global labels are both original, not missing text to reconstruct.",
      "Note8 ends in original unfinished quotation punctuation at the published definition boundary; preserve every word as printed and do not invent a closing quote or intended continuation. Note16 refers to Sikhi while the main poem names Sumedha; preserve the attributed discrepancy without harmonization.",
      "All23 notes remain poem-owned (1–2 heading,3–23 stanza); no chapter heading or summary is assigned. Preserve notes17–23 edition/metre choices and all four independent VRI variant notes. Publisher full refrains do not expand the two VRI peyyāla stanzas."
    ],
