    "mapping_notes": [
      "Complete publisher-edition poem (PTS/BJTS), not a line-complete translation of every VRI stanza. Whole-poem correspondence does not imply segment, line or word equivalence. Preserve independent VRI wording, variant notes and edition differences; do not invent missing words or transfer another poem’s refrain.",
      "Publisher main PTS heading394, BJTS brace/file397 and canonical tha-ap399 remain separate literal identities. The family-death/grief narrative, Sumedha teaching, offerings/praise and named colophons establish this particular pair; no general numbering rule is approved.",
      "Source note28 explicitly calls the offering wording corrupt and records competing readings. Keep its complete published note and chosen flower-stalk translation as attributed editorial judgment, not as a resolution or repair of Pāli.",
      "Source note44 ends in an unclosed original gloss quotation; preserve its exact published words and punctuation and do not invent a closing mark or continuation. Mixed quotation punctuation in note33 also remains unchanged.",
      "All49 notes stay poem-owned (1–2 heading,3–49 stanza); all30 four-line source paragraphs and their two closing colophons are retained. No chapter heading or summary is assigned. Preserve every PTS/BJTS alternative and all seven independent VRI notes; publisher full refrains do not expand the two VRI peyyāla stanzas."
    ],
