    "mapping_notes": [
      "Complete publisher-edition poem (PTS/BJTS), not a line-complete translation of every VRI stanza. Whole-poem correspondence does not imply segment, line or word equivalence. Preserve independent VRI wording, variant notes and edition differences; do not invent missing words or transfer another poem’s refrain.",
      "Publisher main PTS heading404, BJTS brace/file407 and canonical tha-ap409 are separately verified literal identities. The Anoma ascetic, Piyadassi encounter, gem-seat/rose-apple offering, promised retinues and named colophons establish this particular pair, without a general number-offset rule.",
      "Retain four physical eight-line paragraphs with single terminal ranges: local25–26/global4096–4097,27–28/4098–4099,29–30/4100–4101 and32–33/4103–4104. All41 printed stanzas occupy37 physical source paragraphs; do not split or reflow the originals.",
      "All50 notes remain poem-owned (1–2 heading,3–50 stanza); all interpretations, animal/trainer alternatives and metre choices remain attributed. No publisher chapter heading, summary or recitation-marker wording is invented.",
      "The canonical tha-ap409 unit contains an independent recitation marker after its Hemaka colophon, absent from this publisher file. Preserve that original Pāli apparatus separately; whole publisher coverage does not supply an English rendering. All three VRI variant notes and three peyyāla stanzas remain independent and unexpanded."
